Subject: accordion-v2: sticky headers keep sticking, and the content measurement stays on its owner

What: the accordion-v2 root clips with `overflow: clip` instead of `overflow: hidden`,
and the sheet registers `--kb-accordion-content-height` / `--kb-accordion-content-width`
as non-inheriting properties.
Why: `overflow: hidden` makes the root a scroll container, so a `position: sticky`
header inside an item (the kit's StickyAccordionHeader, used by the transcript's
patch and turn-diff accordions) sticks to the root instead of the transcript scroller;
`clip` keeps the rounded-corner clipping without a scroll container. Kobalte writes
the measured content box onto the content element as unregistered (inheriting)
custom properties, which invalidates the inherited style of the whole content
subtree on every write; for a mounted diff that is thousands of elements. The
original accordion sheet registered them; this sheet takes that over.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/accordion-v2.css b/src/v2/components/accordion-v2.css
index 8cd48dbbf4..2d25e1b5ea 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/accordion-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/accordion-v2.css
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
   background: var(--accordion-v2-bg);
   border-radius: var(--radius-md);
   box-shadow: 0 0 0 0.5px var(--accordion-v2-border);
-  overflow: hidden;
+  overflow: clip;
 
   color: var(--accordion-v2-fg);
 
@@ -137,3 +137,22 @@
     height: 0;
   }
 }
+
+/* Kobalte writes the measured content box onto the accordion content element
+   itself, and only that element's own animation ever reads it. Unregistered
+   custom properties inherit, so each of those writes invalidated the inherited
+   style of the ENTIRE content subtree: for a mounted diff that is thousands of
+   elements of recalc for a value nothing below the content ever reads.
+   Registering them as non-inheriting keeps the animations working and confines
+   the invalidation to the one element that owns the value. */
+@property --kb-accordion-content-height {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: false;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
+
+@property --kb-accordion-content-width {
+  syntax: "<length>";
+  inherits: false;
+  initial-value: 0px;
+}
